<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed Abdallah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919–1989</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed Abdallah was a Comorian politician who headed the government of the French Territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> and unilaterally declared its independence on 6 July 1975. Overthrown within weeks, he returned to power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> help in 1978 and ruled as president until he was assassinated in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmed-abdallah.jpg" alt="Ahmed Abdallah" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yanis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portait_officiel_du_pr%C3%A9sident_Abdallah_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
